{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01DNAKEfYqii563aFjJHYTd8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project documents, here's what Anchor is:\n\n- **A personal productivity system** for J.C. Liechty that lives entirely in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) â€” no syncing, no database. Plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files under `domains/`) are the source of truth for tasks, projects, and captured ideas across academic, commercial, family, and writing domains.\n\n- **It ships a self-contained local web app** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a Python stdlib HTTP server that renders an interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` on host PUTER/gwl-server, and reads/writes the markdown directly. Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done / cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored).\n\n- **It ships a matching CLI engine** (`anchor.py`) that mirrors the same logic, generates a static `dashboard.html`, and exposes read-only inspection commands for the R&D surfaces.\n\n- **It has grown a substantial \"R&D control surface\"** layered over the task system â€” a per-project \"cockpit\" for managing trio-driven R&D work (the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio). This is the bulk of recent development, built in four versions:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated AI summaries, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea lane, pinnable deliverables, and an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the one declared native dependency, optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, a stacking window manager, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews, and Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built + merged to master 2026-06-13) â€” each lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) is a tile with one honest status light that expands an inline panel stacking a summary over a resizable xterm.js terminal; adds an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), per-lane doc roles, a cost/tokens/time rollup, grass-to-lane promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **It ships a daily self-test** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that runs at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler, parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed â€” never live model calls), and writes a dated health report, surfacing a red banner on the dashboard if anything failed.\n\n- **It is deliberately dependency-light** â€” Python 3.8+ stdlib only, with the single declared exception of the optional `pywinpty` terminal extra; `distro.py` enforces this by refusing any other native/third-party import in product code.\n\nThe core identity: a **single-folder, markdown-backed, stdlib-only productivity dashboard** that has evolved into a **local mission-control for running and tracking AI-agent R&D projects**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"203ff549-ee33-437c-a62f-825b3eb35dd3","uuid":"51b94861-0d1e-4c72-aecf-c7426f0b3468","request_id":"req_011Cc1egQKK1pDsCR1maFw5G"}
